For those beginning their journey with the
•define-term["pianoforte"]{The full name of the piano, from Italian meaning
"soft-loud," referring to the instrument's dynamic range}, I offer these
foundational principles:

## Posture

Sit with your back straight, feet flat on the floor. Your arms should be
relaxed, wrists level with the keys.

## Hand Position

Curve your fingers as though holding a small ball. The thumb rests on its
side; the other fingers strike with their tips.

## First Exercise

Begin with middle C. Play each white key ascending, saying the note names
aloud: C, D, E, F, G, A, B, C.

This is the foundation of •term["solfège"]: do, re, mi, fa, sol, la, ti, do.

Next week: the black keys and the concept of sharps and flats.
